-- walknet (2.0.9, M 16 Nov 2026, in Westfall's Dust Plains with the arrow to
-- The Fourth Troll Legend in Stranglethorn: "it's not understanding mountains,
-- it wants me to go through the mountain"): the walking net of the Eastern
-- Kingdoms (0) and Kalimdor (1) the arrow follows from one zone to another
-- (Systems/WalkNet.lua). Shortest walks worked out here between the towns,
-- flight points, passes, bridges and road points of each continent on the
-- walking maps of the Forever client (the client's navigation grid,
-- its navigation grid with floors and drops, read as data; SOURCES.txt), once
-- for each faction (keeping clear of the other's towns), cut down to their
-- corners. Only these corner points are in the addon.
-- nodes: "x y " in yards (UnitPosition's frame), in order (node 1, 2, ...).
-- edges: "a b yards cost flags ": the walk a-b, its yards, its yards as the
--   walking maps price them (roads cheaper, steep ground and water dearer),
--   flags = who (1 Alliance, 2 Horde) + 4 if a -> b can be walked + 8 if b -> a
--   (a drop or a waterfall goes one way only).
-- roadnet (2.0.9, M 16 Nov 2026, on Stranglethorn's road facing north with the
-- arrow to the Rebel Camp pointing back: "if I'm on the road, it obviously
-- should let me follow the road"): every road of the walking maps is in the
-- net now (its middle line), not only the roads the town-to-town walks use.
local FDJ = _G.ForeverDungeonJournal_NS
if not FDJ then return end
